  "details": "Whenever one is switching an avatar, the old avatars parameter settings (the 256 synced network bits) are getting used until the wearer has reached a state, where he/she can sync the new intended parameter values (which I assume is up to 1-2 seconds I guess, but thats enough to get into unwanted states). This causes the remote player to see the avatar in unintentional states. This is reproduceable and depending from which avatar one switches from, the destination avatar can receive different states.\nThis issue *may* only occur on faster PCs, which can load avatars as fast as/faster than the wearer. (I assume if someone loads slower than the wearer, it should not be happening)\nSuggestion:\n- add a check which ensures, that the sent parameters are actually from the correct avatar (i think that one might be a bit tricky, maybe you could invalidate the received parameters until the wearer has reached a known state?)\n\nPS: \ndm me on discord @devs, if you want a video/gif of how it looks like: Gireison#0001",
